# The build context of both images is this folder, and the legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0)
# reads only this file. It does not read the Dockerfile.dockerignore beside each Dockerfile, which
# BuildKit prefers, so without this file it would send all of docker/: a target/ folder, a local
# certificate or key, and every other image's folder. An allowlist of what either image needs,
# the union of the two Dockerfile.dockerignore files. The guard's tests are left out: the image
# builds the guard without them.
*
!relay/relay.toml
!relay/open.toml
!rendezvous/manual.toml
!guard/Cargo.toml
!guard/Cargo.lock
!guard/src
guard/src/tests.rs
guard/src/tests
